What:		/sys/bus/platform/devices/*/sci/recover
Date:		August 2026
Contact:	linux-serial@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Write-only recovery control.  Writing "1" while the port is open
		stops transmit, clears stale FIFO and interrupt state, restores
		receive direction, and reactivates a present card.  Normal transmit
		completion never invokes this full recovery.  Normal transactions
		clear stale FIFO state at their start and switch to receive direction
		as soon as the last software byte enters the hardware transmit FIFO.
		Only a refill after the initial FIFO fill repeats the original RX-FIFO
		clear before that switch; a short command does not clear RX twice.
